      "id": 247768,
      "name": "KateWalker",
      "username": "TakeWalker",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-08-31T12:01:03.897Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The funny thing though is that none of them “died” in the traditional sense.</p>\n<p>Erased from existence just means he needs to be drawn back in. Turned into mist? That mist’s still around, at least in one universe.</p>\n<p>This is the kind of thing that is more readily undone in comics. It would feel far less cheap, imo, than just saying, “Oh, they’re not <em>really</em> dead” to someone who, like, got speared through the head or something. Arguments about invalidating sacrifice aside, of course.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2022-08-31T12:01:03.897Z",
      "reply_count": 1,
      "reply_to_post_number": 4,
